hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27596","Abu Qurrah Musa ibn Tariq al-Zubaydi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Umm Khalid bint Khalid, that she heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seek refuge from the punishment of the grave."
"27597","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Said narrated to us, from his father, from Umm Khalid bint Khalid ibn Said ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought clothing containing a small khamisah. He said: Whom do you see most deserving of this? The people fell silent. He said: Bring me Umm Khalid. She was brought, and he dressed her in it, then said to her twice: Wear out and replace, and kept looking at a red or yellow mark on the khamisah, saying: Sanah, sanah, O Umm Khalid - and sanah in Abyssinian speech is: beautiful."
"27598","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, who heard Umm Khalid bint Khalid, he said: I heard no one say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, other than her; she heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seek refuge from the punishment of the grave."
